# Build artifacts - never transfer these, they regenerate
bin/
obj/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Unity - regenerated on first open, and enormous
[Ll]ibrary/
[Tt]emp/
[Oo]bj/
[Bb]uild/
[Bb]uilds/
[Ll]ogs/
[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
*.csproj
*.sln
*.unityproj

# ...but the hand-written test project must travel, or the C# core suite
# can't run on a fresh clone.
!unity/tests/CoreTests/CoreTests.csproj

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Local
*.log

# Screenshots the BONKHORDE test harness writes on each run
bonkhorde/shot-*.png
bonkhorde/sudden.png
# generated by build-artifact.js
*/artifact.html
# every mutated copy of the game is generated: the audit's own _mutant.html,
# and the hand-written ones that exist so a single check can be tested in
# isolation while an audit is already running and holding _mutant.html.
# both are per-process now (_mutant.<pid>.html, _mutant.<pid>.test.js) so two
# audits cannot overwrite each other's game or suite snapshot
bonkhorde/_mutant.*
bonkhorde/_altarprobe.html
# and the throwaway runner that drives one of those, which only lives in this
# directory because it resolves index.html and test.js relative to itself
bonkhorde/mutate[0-9].js
bonkhorde/mutate-results.txt
# The backup taken beside a file before a round edits it, and before a merge
# with the other session's live artifact. The standing rule is that nothing
# substantial is overwritten without a copy beside it; these are those copies,
# a megabyte each, and they are near-duplicates of index.html. Git is the
# thing that remembers old versions - the copies only have to survive the
# session that made them.
bonkhorde/index.pre-*.html
bonkhorde/index.prev.html
bonkhorde/index.l5-mine.html
bonkhorde/test.pre-*.js
bonkhorde/mutate.pre-*.js
bonkhorde/film/*.pre-*.js
build-artifact.pre-*.js
# the hang locator's mutated copy of the game (scratch m36/hang/hang.js) and
# gatemut's per-mutant copies: generated, a megabyte and a half each, deleted
# by the scripts that make them unless they are killed first
bonkhorde/_hang.*
bonkhorde/_gm_*.html
